From a3612217d167772744aacac8be8df8ecd226dc1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harvest <harvest@orinnx.localdomain>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 07:11:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/30] feat(tts): D2-1 shared-engine ctor for slot-pool (share
 read-only engine weights)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Slots 1..N-1 now reuse slot 0's borrowed (read-only) Talker + CodePredictor
ICudaEngines instead of re-deserializing, halving per-slot weight memory.
Per-slot IExecutionContext (kUSER_MANAGED), KV/recurrent cache, RoPE cache,
workspace, Code2Wav, CUDA stream and worker thread stay private — concurrent
slots never contend.

- LLMEngineRunner: getEngine() accessor + borrowed-engine ctor; extract
  initFromEngine() so both ctors share per-instance init (engine via enginePtr()).
- Qwen3OmniTTSRuntime: getTalkerEngine()/getCodePredictorEngine() accessors +
  shared-engine ctor + initializeEngineRunnersShared().
- worker initSlotPool: slot 0 path-ctor, slots 1..N-1 shared-engine ctor;
  removed the DEFERRED fallback to independent path-ctor instances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

